{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And in this matter, etc.</b> One needs to know the intent of His saying ״וּבַדָּבָר הַזֶּה״. And Rashi, of blessed memory, explained that He is speaking about the promise of entering the Land, but this does not appear correct; rather, according to the plain sense of the verse, He is speaking about the wilderness miracles, how HaShem carried them as a man carries his son — for even in this matter they do not believe. And this is your sign: they said (Exodus 17:7) ״הֲיֵשׁ ה׳ בְּקִרְבֵּנוּ אִם אָיִן״. And like the parable that the Zohar brought (Exodus Rabbah 26) about a father who carried his son on his shoulder: they met a certain man and the son was asking him about his father, etc. — so too Israel, the people of HaShem, blessed be He. And this is what is intended by the statement <b>And in this matter, etc.</b> <b>you do not believe in HaShem your Elohim</b> — that He is the One who carries you, etc. And He says <b>who goes</b>, etc. — adding further to specify the details of the matters through which they are obligated to recognize and to believe in HaShem."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:23.057195368Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}